    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS), and the exploration confirms my approach matches the codebase conventions.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the 409-on-duplicate-telephone rule for `POST /api/owners` by adding a uniqueness check step into the existing OfficeFloor pipeline.\n\n**What I added:**\n\n1. **`EnsureTelephoneUnique.java`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 a new pipeline step that runs *after* `ValidateOwnerFields` has normalized the telephone to bare digits. It streams `ownerRepository.findAll()` and compares normalized telephones (stripping non-digits from both sides), throwing a checked `DuplicateTelephoneException` on a match.\n\n2. **`DuplicateTelephoneException.java`** (`rest/escalation/`) \u2014 a checked exception (mirrors the existing `InvalidTelephoneException`).\n\n3. **`DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler.java`** (`rest/escalation/`) \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT` with `{\"errors\":[\"telephone\"]}`, following the existing handler style.\n\n4. **`...DuplicateTelephoneException.yml`** (`officefloor/escalation/`) \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `ensureUniqueTelephone` step (governed by the same `transaction`) between `validate` and `build`.\n\n**Why this placement:** Putting the check after `ValidateOwnerFields` means the comparison uses the already-normalized 10-digit value, and normalizing existing owners' stored telephones on read makes the match robust to formatting differences \u2014 satisfying \"normalized telephone already used by any other owner.\"\n\n**Test results:**\n- `coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone` \u2192 409 \u2713\n- `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone` \u2192 2xx \u2713\n- Full suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, all tests green.",
